Are you sure about that? I can't see "many people", neither speak for them
to believe this or that. What I hear is that many people die because they do
melee in situations when it is inappropriate to do. (You may want to clarify
in what situations it is better to melee than to do ranged attacks; just the
dragons breath attacks come to my mind.) In many other cases it's good to
weaken (or even kill) your enemies before they hurt you. The point is that
proficient ranged attacks (daggers, darts, and spells) are indeed overly
powerful in Nethack, and the misconception is that you can do ranged attacks
even if you're standing adjacent to a monster and do not even need to switch
to your melee weapon. I can't imagine that anyone thinks as melee as a form
of (good or bad) "strategy"; restricting yourself in any way will kill you
more easily. Experienced players will deliberately restrict themselves if
they like, and they will for sure know best when to go for melee or ranged
attacks. And beginners often make the mistake to melee everything.

